* SUPERSEDED: revision-2 netlist of record (sha256 prefix 63ac3d0b7961 before this header line), kept as a record. Revision 3 is r1_safe.spice.
* GENERATED by gen_safe.py -- do not edit; sizes: CREF=0 IH_M=1 ITAIL_M=8 LG=2 LH=8 LIN=2 LM=4 NH=3 RSL=30 RSW=1 WG=2 WH=0.5 WIN=20 WM=16
* r1_safe analog: two window comparators per channel (overcurrent high, negative/phase-short low) with 6-bit
* threshold DACs from VREF. IHP SG13G2, schematic-level SPICE source.
*
* Threshold DAC: one 63-unit rppd string (unit 4 kOhm, w=2 l=30.8) from VREF to VSS, taps T0..T63, Tk = k/63*VREF.
*   Each comparator has two 64:1 thick-NMOS tree multiplexers driven by the same 6 code bits:
*   REFP = T(code), REFN = T(63-code) (bits swapped), so  Vth_od = REFP - REFN = (2*code - 63)/63 * VREF.
*   With r1_isense (Vod = 14*(Vsh - VREF/26)) the shunt-referred threshold is
*   Vsh_th = VREF*(1/26 + (2*code-63)/882): -34.6 mV (code 0) .. +115.4 mV (code 63), 2.381 mV per code,
*   set by VREF and resistor ratios only.
* Comparator r1_safe_cmp: trips (OUT high) when (INP - INN) > (REFP - REFN).
*   Overcurrent: INP=OUTP, INN=OUTN, REFP/REFN from the high code.  Negative/phase short: INP=OUTN, INN=OUTP,
*   REFP=T(63-code_lo), REFN=T(code_lo), i.e. trips when Vod < (2*code_lo - 63)/63*VREF.
*   Inputs are thick-oxide PMOS gates (rated 3.3 V); no divider. The sense outputs are <= VDD by construction.
*   Continuous time, no clock (no clock-edge race as in G1 TRIP F1). Hysteresis by an output-switched current.
*   Output: 1.2 V logic (thick-input inverter on VDD, then a thin-oxide inverter), high = threshold crossed.
* Code bits: 1.2 V logic from r1_ctrl registers, level-shifted here (r1_safe_ls).
* Device conventions: PMOS bulks to VDDA except input pairs (bulk = own tail); NMOS bulks to VSS; mm_ok=1.


